          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Auletta",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Skeleton (Fig. 4 D – E). Ectosome lacking a specialized skeleton. Choanosomal skeleton plumoreticulate, with ascending and longitudinal tracts of strongyles (or strongyloxeas) (Fig. 4 D). Uni- or paucispicular styles are plumo-echinating and connecting tracts (Fig. 4 E). Some terminal tracts of spicules piercing surface in brushes. Spicules (Fig. 5 A – D). Styles (251 – 284.7 – 335 / 2 – 3.5 – 5 µm, length / width): elongated, smooth, slightly curved, blunt and telescopic tips (Fig. 5 A, D); Strongyles (194 – 269.9 – 325 / 3 – 4.6 – 6 µm, length / width): smooth, mostly lightly curved, a few sinuous strongyloxeas are found (Fig. 5 B – C).",
